        "through_line": "I dry-ran steps 1 and 2 against #19809's head `ff13eece89`: 790 = 790, difference 0, 0 bodies changed, sorted. The prose merge conflicts at that one hunk only.",
        "with": "## Landing order: this PR lands first, then #19809 re-runs the re-key on its own pin\n\nOn the maintainer's instruction, this PR lands before #19809. #19809 also edits this file: it re-pins `KanbanConfigSchema` as `Iso882` and raises the count to 790. After this PR has landed, #19809 does this on its own branch:\n\n1. Merge `main`. The pin file conflicts.\n2. Take #19809's own copy of the file, still on the old names, as `F`: run `git show H:packages/spec/src/type-alias-convention.pin.test.ts > F`, where `H` is #19809's head before the merge. Then run the transform below on `F`. It renames and sorts every pin, including the new one, which becomes `Iso_ui_view__KanbanConfigSchema`.\n   - This step is exact while #19809's pin set is `main`'s set plus its own pin. At `ff13eece89` it is: 790 pins, which are `main`'s 789 plus `ui/view.zod.ts::KanbanConfigSchema`.\n3. Re-apply this PR's prose half as a three-way file merge: `git merge-file -p F BASE1 HEAD1 > out`. `BASE1` is this file at `ece9f71d2c`. `HEAD1` is this file at `fc8eda2d62`, which is the same bytes `main` holds once this PR lands.\n4. By hand:\n   - In the one conflicting hunk, at the tail of the count history, keep both entries: this PR's `789 -> 789` entry first, then #19809's entry restated as `789 -> 790`, with its `toHaveLength(790)`. In that entry, name the pin `Iso_ui_view__KanbanConfigSchema` instead of `Iso882`.\n   - In #19809's `ui/view` note, name the pin `Iso_ui_view__KanbanConfigSchema` instead of `Iso882`, and drop \"Iso829 stays vacant\".\n5. Check acceptance: compare `readIsomorphicPins` on `F` before the transform with the result. The sets must be equal, the bodies unchanged, the names on the rule, and the block sorted.\n\nI dry-ran steps 2 and 3 against #19809's head `ff13eece89`: 790 = 790, set difference 0 both ways, 0 bodies changed, 0 names off the rule, sorted, and `Iso_ui_view__KanbanConfigSchema` declared once. The prose merge conflicts at that one hunk only.\n",
